# Rank 1230 / CVE-2024-23897: Jenkins builds every CLI command's argument parser
# with the args4j default:
#
#   protected CmdLineParser getCmdLineParser() {
#       return new CmdLineParser(this);
#   }
#
# args4j's "at-syntax" is on unless the caller says otherwise: an argument of the
# form `@path` is replaced, before option parsing, by the lines of the file that
# path names. The Jenkins CLI accepts commands over HTTP and over the remoting
# channel, so anyone who can reach that endpoint can name a server-side file and
# read its contents back out of the parser's own error message -- CWE-22 plus
# CWE-200. The fixed revision adds `CLICommand.ALLOW_AT_SYNTAX`, a boolean read from
# the `hudson.cli.CLICommand.allowAtSyntax` system property and therefore false
# unless an administrator opts in, and threads it through
# `ParserProperties.defaults().withAtSyntax(ALLOW_AT_SYNTAX)` into both parser
# constructions -- `CLICommand.getCmdLineParser()` and `CLIRegisterer`'s
# `bindMethod`. Its Security3314Test asserts the argument `@<tempfile>` is echoed
# back verbatim instead of the file's contents.
#
# Detection needs vocabulary for the weakness, because nothing is labelled:
# `vyql match` on the vulnerable file reported no source, no sink and no control.
# The shape is the one `code.XmlParserCreate` / `core.XmlHardening` model
# for XXE -- a library default that is only safe while nobody feeds the API
# untrusted input, plus the documented call that turns the default off -- so it is
# expressed the same way:
#
#   code.ArgumentFileExpansion (issue)          a command-line parser that expands
#                                               @-prefixed arguments into file
#                                               contents
#   core.ArgumentFileExpansionControl (check)   the expansion mode is set
#                                               explicitly instead of inherited
#   path.ArgumentFileExpansionUnrestricted      the threat kind both refer to
#   VYQL-PATH-061                               fires on the first unless the
#                                               second covers its endpoint or path
#
# The bindings name only what args4j documents (`vyql/bindings/java/m420f6b67.vyql`,
# argumentFileExpansion465 and argumentFileExpansionControl466): constructing a
# `CmdLineParser` expands @-arguments, and `withAtSyntax` is the switch. Coverage is
# by the presence of the switch rather than by its argument value, because the fixed
# revision
# passes a field (`ALLOW_AT_SYNTAX`), not a literal -- once a codebase sets the mode
# at all, the value is its own decision and not the library's default.
#
# The rule keeps the judgement: an argument parser is only a file-read primitive
# when its arguments come from somewhere the caller does not control, so it is
# medium severity with a low confidence floor, in the same register as
# VYQL-DESER-004 over `newDocumentBuilder()`.
#
# Real checkout, bounded, on the vulnerable revision (jenkins is large enough that a
# whole-repo scan does not fit the 180s bound, so the scan targets the module
# holding the changed files): `vyql scan --max-ram 4GB
# core/src/main/java/hudson/cli` reports 1 finding, VYQL-PATH-061 at
# CLICommand.java:310 -- the `new CmdLineParser(this)` the advisory names. The
# patched form of the same function clears it.
#
# The fixed revision's second site, `CLIRegisterer.bindMethod`, is not reported, and the cause
# is not this rule: it sits inside an anonymous class body (`new
# CloneableCLICommand() { ... }`), and the Java frontend extracts nothing from
# those. The fourth and fifth cases below are the isolating pair -- identical
# statements, differing only in whether the enclosing class is named or anonymous;
# the named one reports VYQL-PATH-061 and the anonymous one reports nothing. The
# same pair holds for an unrelated sink: `Runtime.getRuntime().exec(v)` is labelled
# `code.CommandExecution` in a named class and labelled nothing inside `new
# Runnable() { ... }`. This is the Java twin of the PHP anonymous-class gap
# recorded for rank 1194, and it is entered in ENGINE-GAPS.md rather than worked
# around here.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed
#
# vyql/ontology/concepts/code/ArgumentFileExpansion.vyql,
# vyql/ontology/concepts/core/ArgumentFileExpansionControl.vyql,
# vyql/ontology/threatkinds/path/ArgumentFileExpansionUnrestricted.vyql,
# vyql/packs/path/vypr/path/ArgumentFileExpansionUnrestricted.vyql (VYQL-PATH-061),
# vyql/bindings/java/m420f6b67.vyql (argumentFileExpansion465,
# argumentFileExpansionControl466). OWASP Java and Python unchanged at +1.00 and
# +0.90; neither corpus nor the RealVuln corpus contains args4j.

test "rank1230: a CLI command parser built on the args4j default expands @-file arguments"
  lang java
  file CLICommand.java
  expect VYQL-PATH-061
  code
  ```
  package hudson.cli;

  import java.util.List;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.CmdLineParser;

  public abstract class CLICommand {

      protected CmdLineParser getCmdLineParser() {
          return new CmdLineParser(this);
      }

      public int run(List<String> args) throws Exception {
          CmdLineParser parser = getCmdLineParser();
          parser.parseArgument(args.toArray(new String[0]));
          return 0;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1230: setting the at-syntax mode explicitly clears the finding"
  lang java
  file CLICommand.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-061
  code
  ```
  package hudson.cli;

  import java.util.List;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.CmdLineParser;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.ParserProperties;
  import jenkins.util.SystemProperties;

  public abstract class CLICommand {

      public static boolean ALLOW_AT_SYNTAX = SystemProperties.getBoolean(CLICommand.class.getName() + ".allowAtSyntax");

      protected CmdLineParser getCmdLineParser() {
          ParserProperties properties = ParserProperties.defaults().withAtSyntax(ALLOW_AT_SYNTAX);
          return new CmdLineParser(this, properties);
      }

      public int run(List<String> args) throws Exception {
          CmdLineParser parser = getCmdLineParser();
          parser.parseArgument(args.toArray(new String[0]));
          return 0;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1230: a parser built from ParserProperties that never touches at-syntax still expands @-file arguments"
  lang java
  file CLICommand.java
  expect VYQL-PATH-061
  code
  ```
  package hudson.cli;

  import org.kohsuke.args4j.CmdLineParser;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.ParserProperties;

  public abstract class CLICommand {

      protected CmdLineParser getCmdLineParser() {
          ParserProperties properties = ParserProperties.defaults().withUsageWidth(120);
          return new CmdLineParser(this, properties);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1230: the same construction in a named class is reported"
  lang java
  file CLIRegisterer.java
  expect VYQL-PATH-061
  code
  ```
  package hudson.cli.declarative;

  import java.util.List;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.CmdLineParser;

  public class CLIRegisterer {

      static class Command extends CloneableCLICommand {
          private CmdLineParser bindMethod(List<MethodBinder> binders) {
              CmdLineParser parser = new CmdLineParser(null);
              return parser;
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1230: the Java frontend extracts nothing from an anonymous class body, so the same construction there is not reported"
  lang java
  file CLIRegisterer.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-061
  code
  ```
  package hudson.cli.declarative;

  import java.util.List;
  import org.kohsuke.args4j.CmdLineParser;

  public class CLIRegisterer {

      Object discover() {
          return new CloneableCLICommand() {
              private CmdLineParser bindMethod(List<MethodBinder> binders) {
                  CmdLineParser parser = new CmdLineParser(null);
                  return parser;
              }
          };
      }
  }
  ```
